// Signing configuration for the app target.
//
// I keep my actual Apple team / identity out of this open-source repo. The
// real values live in Secrets.xcconfig (git-ignored). The include below is
// optional — if that file isn't present (anyone building from source), the
// build just signs ad-hoc / "to run locally", which is fine for them.
//
// Why this matters: macOS remembers the "access data from other apps" grant
// only for a stable signing identity. Ad-hoc builds get a new identity every
// launch, so macOS re-asks every time. A real (even Development) identity in
// Secrets.xcconfig makes the grant stick between launches.
#include? "Secrets.xcconfig"
